### Search — every query shape, against the seeded demo corpus.
# 50 clients, 126 documents. Every response carries X-Total-Count.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@apiKey = dev-only-insecure-key-do-not-use-in-production-env

### Identity: an email fragment. Client first, match.tier = identity.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=NevisWealth&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Identity: a first name shared by two clients. Both are returned.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=John&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Category: a KYC purpose. Documents only, zero clients.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=tax%20residency&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Category: wording the documents never use.
# The completion statements are tagged source_of_funds, so they lead.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=source%20of%20funds&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Category where a client legitimately also matches, but must not outrank.
# Grace Kim's description says "advisory arrangements", which scores 0.64.
# The engagement letters come first; she appears below them on the context tier.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=advisory%20fees&limit=15
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Compound: a client plus a category.
# The client is the qualifier and the document is the target, so John Doe's
# utility bill leads, then his other matching documents, then John himself,
# then other clients' bills.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=John%20Doe%20utility%20bill&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Compound with a possessive. Bill Carter's statement first, then Bill.
# "Bill" is also a synonym for utility_bill; the possessive resolves the ambiguity.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=Bill's%20statement&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### The same token without the possessive is read as a category.
# Expect the client Bill Carter first on an identity hit, then the bills.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=bill&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### A misspelled name still scopes a compound query.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=Hendersen%20council%20tax&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Out of domain. Expect 200 with an empty array, not the least-bad match.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=best%20pizza%20recipes%20in%20Naples
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Paging. The order is total, so a page is a slice; ids never repeat.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=proof%20of%20address&limit=5&offset=0
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=proof%20of%20address&limit=5&offset=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Deep page, well past the end. Expect 200, an empty array, and a non-zero X-Total-Count.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=proof%20of%20address&limit=5&offset=500
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
